The tension at the lowest point is $\mathrm{T}=\frac{\mathrm{mv}^2}{\mathrm{r}}+\mathrm{mg}$ To complete the vertical circle, the minimum velocity should be $\mathrm{v}=\sqrt{5 \mathrm{gr}} \begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad$\mathrm{T}$ \text{ and } =\frac{\mathrm{m}(\sqrt{5 \mathrm{gr}})^2}{\mathrm{r}}+\mathrm{mg}\\
\mathrm{R}$& =5 $\mathrm{mg}+\mathrm{mg}\\
\therefore \quad \mathrm{T}$& =6 $\mathrm{mg}
\end{aligned}$
